# XSH call_once()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Racing callers, the signal case: the page's recursion, longjmp and
# cancellation notes are undefined or CX-cancel (not tested).
# Every once_flag has static storage and ONCE_FLAG_INIT.

assertion  XSH.call_once.001
anchor     functions/call_once.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       For each once_flag, the first call_once() runs init_routine and
           later calls with the same flag (from the same thread or another)
           do not run it again; a second flag has its own first call.
test       t/001-once.c

assertion  XSH.call_once.002
anchor     functions/call_once.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       Four threads calling call_once() together with one flag all return
           only after init_routine (200 ms long) has completed, and it ran
           once; each then sees the plain data init_routine wrote.
test       t/002-race.c

assertion  XSH.call_once.003
anchor     functions/call_once.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       A thread waiting in call_once() while another thread's
           init_routine runs, and taking a caught signal (SIGUSR1, no
           SA_RESTART), still returns only after init_routine has completed.
note       The signal comes 100 ms into a 600 ms initialization.
test       t/003-signal.c

assertion  XSH.call_once.004
anchor     functions/call_once.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       A thread with a deferred cancellation request pending calls
           call_once() with an init_routine that has no cancellation point:
           the call returns and the routine ran once; the thread is canceled
           only at its next pthread_testcancel().
test       t/004-not-cancel-point.c

assertion  XSH.call_once.005
anchor     functions/call_once.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       When init_routine is canceled at a cancellation point, the next
           call_once() with the flag calls init_routine again (it runs a
           second time) and returns.
test       t/005-canceled-init.c
